  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "The position $s(t)$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=3{t}^{2}-12t,\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle when $t=1.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-12t) \\\\  & =6t-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $t=1,$ the velocity is\n\n$$\nv(1)=6(1)-12=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed is $|-6|=6.$",
